tel 1.0 specification.tel/tels:1.0.0
name lock

# Draft TEL schema for build.lock (fury.md §12; builds.md §9.2): a verifiable
# memoization of resolution, with authority over exactly one thing — when the world
# was sampled. One entry per (coordinate, selector) that resolution touched across the
# whole declared space, so different cases resolving different selectors of one module
# coexist. Each entry is a distribution.md §5 Release record with its inclusion proof
# against a signed tree head recorded once per directory. Written deterministically
# (entries sorted by coordinate then selector; proofs in leaf order) so diffs are
# meaningful. A selector in build.tel with no entry, or an entry whose selector no
# longer matches, is a stale lock: an error unless --update.

scalar Coordinate
  description  A <domain>/<name> index coordinate
  validate     module-ref

scalar Selector
  description  A version prefix x[.y[.z]], or a tag-name where not version-shaped (§12.6)
  validate     selector

scalar Hash
  description  A domain-separated hash (spec §7.1), as the format prints it
  validate     hash

# The signed tree head (distribution.md §4) the entries below were proved against.
record Head
  description  One directory's tree head at sampling time

  field directory String
  field size String
  field root Hash
  field sampled String

# The bounded Release record (distribution.md §5) plus its Merkle proof.
record Entry
  description  One resolution, `<kind> <coordinate> <selector>`, and the release it landed on

  field coordinate Coordinate
  field selector Selector
  field version String optional
  field snapshot Hash
  field manifest Hash
  field payload Hash
  field location String
  field publisher Hash
  field directory String
  field leaf String
  field proof Hash optional repeatable

document
  field head Head optional repeatable
  field dependency Entry optional repeatable  # include selectors
  field tool Entry optional repeatable        # tool version selectors (builds.md §9.1 gap 1)
  field component Entry optional repeatable   # per-edge component selectors
  field host Entry optional repeatable        # host-contract tag resolutions (hosts.md §3)
  field registry Entry optional repeatable    # registry layers (fury.md §7)
